  "thought": "The layer rank views reveal strong patterns. The top latency layers are all layer0_ffn1_tiling0-7 (each ~2.84s), and the critical-end layers are dominated by layer0_ffn2_tiling0-15 and layer0_norm2/res2. The aggregate breakdown shows compute is 68% of time but only 23% of energy, while memory is 43% and communication is 34% of energy. The ffn1 tilings dominate latency_sum and energy, while ffn2 tilings dominate critical-end position. I should also check operator groups to see if attention or other groups are significant, and get the execution timeline to understand idle gaps and core utilization.",
  "action": "tool",
  "tool": {
    "name": "summarize_operator_groups",
    "arguments": {
      "sort_by": "latency_sum",
      "top_groups": 8,
      "include_components": true
    }
  }
}

